title: No quick fix for NoMatchingSymbol relocation hints (string::Join->Text::Join, Draw::*->Display::*)
updated_at: "2026-08-31T11:25:54Z"
---
## Expected Behavior

A `NoMatchingSymbol` diagnostic that carries a relocation hint (structured
`hint` field: `string::Join` → `Text::Join`, `string::Repeat` →
`Text::Repeat`, `Draw::GetWidth` → `Display::GetWidth`, …) should offer a
code action that rewrites the qualified callee to the hinted name — the
hint is already data (a qualified name), not prose.

## Actual Behavior

`did_you_mean` matches only `unknown type`/`undefined identifier`
messages; the `removed_api` family drives only `RemovedApiUsage` (member
path). Nothing claims `NoMatchingSymbol`, so relocations are hint-text
only. Pre-existing gap for `Draw::*`; extended to `string::Join`/`Repeat`
by GH #18 (see `removed_api_hint` in src/typecheck/checker.rs).

## Notes

- The near-name (typo) hints share the same `hint` field and are equally
  valid rename targets; one fix family can serve both.
- Needs the structured kind at code-action time (message parsing is
  forbidden per removed_api.rs doctrine) — check what FixContext exposes.

## Test cases

- `string::Join(...)` on a 1.29.14 typedb → action rewriting to
  `Text::Join`, call shape untouched (same-arity rename).
- `Draw::GetWidth()` on 1.29.5 → action rewriting to `Display::GetWidth`.
- Negative: NoMatchingSymbol with no hint → no action offered.